reference.api:
```
POST /v1/tweets                {text, media_ids?}          → 201 {tweet_id}
POST /v1/users/{id}/follow                                  → 204
GET  /v1/timeline/home?cursor=&limit=50                     → {tweets[], next_cursor}
GET  /v1/users/{id}/tweets?cursor=&limit=50                 → {tweets[], next_cursor}
```
- Cursor is the last tweet id (ids are time-sortable), not an offset, so new posts do not shift pages.
- `POST /tweets` carries a client-generated idempotency key to survive retries.
